            "subject": "LU-20515 lnet: prevent peer net list corruption during discovery"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-21 20:12:15.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-22 01:37:46.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20515 tests: merge a new NID into a locked peer",
        "message": "LU-20515 tests: merge a new NID into a locked peer\n\nA server adds an interface. Lustre then registers the new NID with\nLNetAddPeer() before discovery tells the client about it. The client\nmakes a peer for the new NID and merges it into the locked peer of\nthe primary NID. That locked peer can have more than one NID. Then the\nmerge corrupts the peer lists, and peer teardown fails an assertion\nin lnet_destroy_peer_locked().\n\nAdd sanity-lnet test 42. It adds a third interface on one node and\ndrops the discovery push. It then registers the new NID with\nadd_uuid. The test checks that the locked peer gets the new NID and\nthat LNet shuts down cleanly.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Id305603405ff3fd1587caab53b2c3c1e0edac6bd\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
